Venetium 0070 - Lumia Adreno: tile rasterization back on the CPU (scrolling drew old text over the page).
1. With v1.3.1.2 on the Lumia 735 (Adreno 305, driver 9.14.1140, D3D11 feature level 9_3), scrolling drew text from
   two scroll positions over each other; a tab switch, which rasters every tile again into fresh textures, cleaned it
   up until the next scroll. It does not happen on WARP at 9_3 (headless or in a real window, with the ARM32 9_3
   paths on), so it is this driver.
2. Device test of five switches on v1.3.1.2 (community report 2026-11-04): --disable-gpu-rasterization fixes it on
   every page; --flush_on_framebuffer_change fixes text-only pages (chrome://gpu) but not Google search;
   --disable_discard_framebuffer, --disable-partial-raster and --ui-disable-partial-swap change nothing. So the fault
   is GPU tile rasterization on this driver (the tab-switch cure points at reused tile textures keeping old content);
   GPU compositing, which stayed on in that test, is fine.
3. The Lumias rastered on the GPU only because of the exception 0051 added to software_rendering_list.json entry 122
   (0067 widened it to every Lumia GPU id); upstream, that entry blocklists GPU tile rasterization on Windows GPUs
   below ps_5.0 + Direct3D11. This patch removes the exception, so the Lumias fall under entry 122 again, which is
   what --disable-gpu-rasterization did in the test. Nothing else changes: the Gr shader disk cache stays on (0036),
   and --enable-gpu-rasterization still turns GPU rasterization back on for testing. The exception's note on the
   Lumia GPU ids moves to gpu_driver_bug_list.json entry 487, which uses the same ids and pointed at it (comment
   only: the generated driver bug list code is unchanged).

diff --git a/gpu/config/gpu_driver_bug_list.json b/gpu/config/gpu_driver_bug_list.json
--- a/gpu/config/gpu_driver_bug_list.json
+++ b/gpu/config/gpu_driver_bug_list.json
@@ -3817,7 +3817,7 @@
