-      "comment": "Venetium 0067: on the Lumia 735 (Windows RT 8.1, qcdx9um8974.dll 9.14.1140) the GPU process crashed 1-2 s after start, in all 3 dumps at qcdx9um8974+0x890f5, writing past the end of a buffer: viz::SkiaOutputDeviceGL::Present -> gl::GLSurfacePresentationHelper::PreSwapBuffers -> gl::GPUTimer::QueryTimeStamp -> glBeginQueryEXT(GL_TIME_ELAPSED_EXT) -> ANGLE rx::Query11::resume -> ID3D11DeviceContext::Begin(D3D11_QUERY_TIMESTAMP_DISJOINT) -> D3D10Level9 -> qcdx9um8974 (D3D11 at feature level 9_x runs through the D3D9 user-mode driver). After 3 crashes Chromium turns the GPU off and everything is software. Without GL_EXT_disjoint_timer_query the presentation helper uses a fence (a D3D11 event query) instead, and WebGL does not offer the timer extensions. Device ids: every Lumia GPU, from the driver INFs in github.com/WOA-Project/Lumia-Drivers (see software_rendering_list.json entry 122, Venetium 0051/0067).",
+      "comment": "Venetium 0067: on the Lumia 735 (Windows RT 8.1, qcdx9um8974.dll 9.14.1140) the GPU process crashed 1-2 s after start, in all 3 dumps at qcdx9um8974+0x890f5, writing past the end of a buffer: viz::SkiaOutputDeviceGL::Present -> gl::GLSurfacePresentationHelper::PreSwapBuffers -> gl::GPUTimer::QueryTimeStamp -> glBeginQueryEXT(GL_TIME_ELAPSED_EXT) -> ANGLE rx::Query11::resume -> ID3D11DeviceContext::Begin(D3D11_QUERY_TIMESTAMP_DISJOINT) -> D3D10Level9 -> qcdx9um8974 (D3D11 at feature level 9_x runs through the D3D9 user-mode driver). After 3 crashes Chromium turns the GPU off and everything is software. Without GL_EXT_disjoint_timer_query the presentation helper uses a fence (a D3D11 event query) instead, and WebGL does not offer the timer extensions. Device ids: the Lumia GPU drivers' own, from their INFs in github.com/WOA-Project/Lumia-Drivers: an ACPI display adapter's DXGI ids are its ACPI hardware id read as two little-endian fourccs, so ACPI QCOM246F = vendor 0x4d4f4351 ('QCOM') + device 0x46363432 ('246F'), which is what d3dprobe measured on the Adreno 330 (community reports 2026-10-11 and 2026-11-01). Every Lumia GPU from Windows Phone 8.1 on is QCOM246F: 8974 Adreno 330 (1520, 930, Icon, 2520), 8x26 Adreno 305 (730/735, 830), 8x12 Adreno 302, 8909 Adreno 304 (550, 650), 8992/8994 Adreno 418/430 (950, 950 XL). The Windows Phone 8.0 chips have their own ids: 8960 Adreno 225 (920, 1020; QCOM2002 = 0x32303032) and 8930/8x27 Adreno 305 (520, 620, 720; QCOM0300 = 0x30303330). Venetium 0070 moved this note here from software_rendering_list.json entry 122 when it removed the 0051/0067 GPU rasterization exception for these ids.",
